        type: "p",
        text: "Scammers target tourists in every popular destination. Being aware prevents most losses. Common scams worldwide: 1) Fake taxi meters — driver claims meter broken, charges inflated rate. Prevention: Use rideshare apps, agree price before entering. 2) Friendship bracelet/rose scam — person approaches, ties bracelet or hands rose, then demands money. Prevention: Keep walking, don't accept anything. 3) Spilled liquid/mustard scam — liquid spilled on you, helpful stranger helps clean, steals wallet. Prevention: Clean yourself, walk away. 4) Fake police — plainclothes 'officers' demand to see passport/wallet, steal money. Prevention: Insist on going to police station, never hand over wallet. 5) ATM helper — friendly local 'helps' with ATM, steals card/PIN. Prevention: Refuse help, use ATMs inside banks. 6) Free friendship ring/tea ceremony — locals invite for tea, then demand exorbitant payment. Prevention: Refuse unsolicited invitations. 7) Fake booking websites — counterfeit hotel/tour sites take payment, no booking made. Prevention: Book through Booking.com, Agoda, verify with hotel directly. 8) Closed attraction scam — 'guide' says attraction closed, offers alternative tour (commission shop). Prevention: Verify yourself, ignore touts. 9) Camera drop — scammer drops broken camera, blames tourist, demands payment. Prevention: Walk away firmly. 10) Wallet drop — 'found' wallet offered to share, distraction theft. Prevention: Don't engage. General rule: If something feels off, walk away. Politeness can wait — your safety comes first.",
