        text: "Editing transforms good photos into great ones. Best editing apps: 1) Adobe Lightroom Mobile (free, premium USD 10/month) — professional, powerful. 2) Snapseed (free, Google) — excellent free option, intuitive. 3) VSCO (free, premium USD 20/year) — film-inspired presets. 4) Lightroom CC Desktop (USD 10/month with Photoshop) — professional standard. 5) Capture One (USD 29/month) — professional alternative to Lightroom. Basic editing workflow: 1) Crop and straighten — fix composition. 2) Exposure — adjust brightness. 3) Contrast — increase for punch, decrease for flat look. 4) Highlights — recover blown-out skies. 5) Shadows — open up dark areas. 6) White balance — adjust warmth/coolness. 7) Vibrance — boost muted colors (better than saturation). 8) Clarity/texture — add mid-tone contrast. 9) Sharpening — final touch. 10) Noise reduction — for high ISO. Advanced techniques: 1) Local adjustments (graduated filter, radial filter, adjustment brush) — edit specific areas. 2) HSL panel — adjust individual colors. 3) Tone curve — fine-tune contrast. 4) Presets — save favorite settings. Common beginner mistakes: 1) Over-saturating — natural looks better. 2) Too much clarity — looks harsh. 3) Over-sharpening — artificial look. 4) Heavy HDR — fake look. 5) Too many filters — distracting. Goal: Enhance photo to look natural, not obviously edited.",
